  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 329 AM EDT Thu Oct 22 2026\n\nAnother calm, clear night is producing optimal conditions for \nradiational cooling. Temperatures are in the 40s in most areas and \nwill continue to settle into the upper 30s and lower 40s through \ndaybreak. Our coolest rural, sheltered low spots in the Bluegrass \nand Lake Cumberland regions could see mid 30s and patchy frost early \nthis morning. \n\nRecent satellite imagery shows the development of river valley fog \nacross eastern KY, a trend that will expand into central KY through \nthe pre-dawn hours. The fog may become locally dense between 5-9 AM \nEDT, mainly along the river valleys. Fog should largely dissipate by \nmid-morning, and another round of valley fog looks likely early \nFriday. \n\nOur stretch of spectacular weather continues today. An upper level \nridge is positioned over the central CONUS, with upper troughing \nover each coast. Broad high pressure at the surface, centered off to \nour N and NW, is contributing to a dry airmass and persistent NE low-\nlevel flow. In the short term, the upper level ridge is forecast to \ndrift slowly eastward toward the MS Valley while sfc high pressure \nstrengthens as it shifts southeast across the eastern US and Canada. \nRidging, both at the surface and aloft, will then build over our \nregion through the weekend and into early next week. \n\nStubborn high pressure and a notably dry airmass give us high \nconfidence in dry weather through next Wednesday. In short, largely \ndry weather is likely through the last several days of October. \nTemperatures will be fairly steady over the next week as well, with \nafternoon highs ranging from the upper 60s and lower 70s in the \nBluegrass to the low/mid 70s elsewhere. Overnight temps will dip \ninto the upper 30s to mid 40s. Friday and Saturday mornings both \nhave patchy frost potential, especially in rural, low-lying areas. \n\nIt is unclear when our next chance for appreciable rainfall will be. \nA frontal system could bring a brief shot for light rain by late \nnext week or over Halloween weekend, but confidence in this is very \nlow at this time. Again, mainly dry weather is expected through the \nend of the month.",
